<title>HONG KONG: Chairman cuts Interform stake by 2.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Chairman cuts Interform stake by 2.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interform Ceramics Technologies Ltd said on Tuesday that its chairman Ngan Man Po had sold 18 million shares, or 2.53 percent of the company issued share capital, on September 27.</p>
<p>Ngan's Great Chance Holdings Ltd held 62.49 percent of the ceramics production lines supplier as in January 1996. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>Interform shares ended one cent down at HK$0.64 per share on Tuesday on volume of 5.05 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
